// [Claude, 2026-10-09] _sigma0_tau051_100k: as bogner3_r075_deep_s32_eqfull_vtk_strict_mom2_sigma0_100k_gas.prm with relaxationRateOverride 1.96078431 (tau 0.51) (see gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py).
// [Claude, 2026-10-09] _strict_mom2_sigma0_100k: as bogner3_r075_deep_s32_eqfull_vtk_strict_mom2_sigma0_gas.prm, 100000 steps, VTK steps of the 100k runs (see gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py).
// [Claude, 2026-10-09] _strict_mom2_sigma0: as bogner3_r075_deep_s32_eqfull_vtk_strict_mom2_gas.prm with surfaceTensionOverride 0 (see gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py).
// [Claude, 2026-10-09] _strict_mom2: as bogner3_r075_deep_s32_eqfull_vtk_strict_mom_gas.prm with its own snapshot folder, for the [MOMENTUM-STAGES] run (see gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py).
// [Claude, 2026-10-09] _strict_mom: as bogner3_r075_deep_s32_eqfull_vtk_strict_gas.prm, 25000 steps, logMomentumBudget true (see gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py).
// [Claude, 2026-10-08] GENERATED by gen_bogner3_eqfull_vtk_prms.py from bogner3_r075_deep_s32_100k_gas.prm (thesis run): whole-domain VTK with velocity,
// periodic in x and y (N/S walls removed), seeding as before 2026-10-01, own snapshot folder; timesteps and start
// position unchanged.
// bogner3_r075_deep_s32_100k_gas.prm -- hand-edited copy of bogner3_r075_deep_s32_gas.prm, SINGLE CONTINUOUS 100k-step variant (see next line)
// [Claude, 2026-09-29] HAND-EDIT (per "run it again from timestep 0", i.e. a SINGLE CONTINUOUS run to 100000 steps, no resume in the
// middle): job 4273525 (fresh, 51000 steps) settled at 26.56+-0.03 deg for its last ~20000 steps; job 4273559 (RESUMED from 4273525's
// checkpoint at step 50001, out to 100000) left that lock within ~1000 steps of resuming, with a large warning burst right at the
// resume point -- unresolved whether that reflects the state's own long-run instability or an artifact of the checkpoint reload.
// This run tests that directly: identical setup, but ONE continuous execution from step 0 to 100000 (checkpointing still happens at
// snapshotFrequency=50000 for safety, but nothing LOADS from it mid-run, so there is no save/reload discontinuity to suspect).
// Original header follows unmodified below (box/basin/physics/guard all unchanged, only timesteps/density-column window/snapshot
// folder differ): [Claude, 2026-09-29] HAND-EDIT (per "we haven't tried s=32 for the free box yet, try this for the 0.75 version, run it for 51k,
// checkpoint every 50k"): box DOUBLED to Bogner's own high-resolution size s=32 (halfExtents <16,32,16> = 32x64x32, was s=16 =
// 16x32x16) -- his own basin doubles from 130x40x40 to 260x80x80 when he goes from s=16 to s=32, so the WHOLE BASIN is doubled here
// too (domainSize 192x90x120, was 96x45x60; liquidHeightFactor 10.0, was 5.0 -> absoluteLiquidHeight=60.0746, was 30.0673) to keep
// the same relative clearances (box-to-wall, box-to-floor) as the s=16/s=18 runs, not just the box itself. cellsPerBlock unchanged
// <16,15,15> -> 12x6x8 = 576 ranks (was 72), same multinode scale already used for the sphere resolution scan (run_576_pinres_sphere_
// R4.sbatch, but with cellsPerBlock <32,15,15> -> 6x6x8=288 ranks/4 nodes, not <16,15,15> -> 576/8 nodes, per explicit request to use
// 4 nodes). [Claude, 2026-09-29] FIX (job 4273521's own first attempt at this ran at g_SI ~= 78, not 9.81, and filled the WHOLE
// domain with liquid -- see its retraction in THESIS_PLAN.md): bedCopiesInX/Y doubled (1 -> 2) to match the doubled domainSize, so
// avgParticleDiameter/dx_SI/dt_SI come back out IDENTICAL to every s=16/s=18 run (getAvgDiameterScalingFactor, Utility.h: scaling
// depends on domainSize / bedCopies, not on domainSize alone). gravityOverride is UNCHANGED (5.06585e-05): it is a pure dx_SI/dt_SI
// unit-conversion constant tied to the sediment-bed particle scale, NOW genuinely domain-independent again with this fix, tied to
// particle scale, not to domain/box size, so 'real g_SI=9.81' means the same lattice value regardless of resolution here. Heave
// recomputed for s=32 at the new level 60.0746, seed 2.86 deg -> z_c=52.085. Only 51000 steps (cheap first look, not a full 100k/
// 150k run, given the 8x cell-count cost of doubling every dimension); single checkpoint at snapshotFrequency=50000. Real g_SI=9.81,
// guard off (unchanged), no VTK. Free heave + X/Y translation, roll about Y only (pinRotationAxes <1,0,1>).
// Free heave + X/Y translation, roll about Y only (pinRotationAxes <1,0,1>). Eval sqlite (totalFluidMass, maxFluidPos_z) every 250 steps is kept by the job.
// ---- original header follows ----
// bognerlike_r075_h286_gas.prm -- generated by gen_bognerlike_box_scan.py (do not hand-edit)
// [Claude, 2026-09-28] Bogner-like FREE box at real g_SI=9.81: basin <96,45,40> (depth ~20), box 18x36x18 rho 0.75, seed heel 2.86 deg, heave 15.506,
// free heave + X/Y translation, roll about Y only (pinRotationAxes <1,0,1>), 100000 steps, force log every 250. Derived from prms/pinbox_r075_a10_gas.prm.
// ---- original header follows ----
// pinbox_r075_a10_gas.prm -- generated by gen_pinned_box_scan.py (do not hand-edit)
// [Claude, 2026-09-28] fully PINNED 30x60x30 box, rho 0.75, heel 10.0 deg, heave 52.814, real g_SI=9.81, 12000 steps; density column x=y=5 over 10000-11999.
// Derived from prms/pinscan_sphere_R24_real_f075_gas.prm (sphere block replaced). See gen_pinned_box_scan.py.
// ---- original header follows ----
// pinscan_sphere_R24_real_f075_gas.prm  -- generated by gen_pinned_sphere_scan.py (do not hand-edit)
// [Claude, 2026-09-28] FULLY PINNED sphere r=24 at z=51.548 (nominal submerged fraction 0.75, waterline 59.8831),
// real gravity, still water, 12000 steps. Measures mean MEM F_hydro_z ([FloaterForces], every 250 steps)
// vs rho*g*V_sub to test the g-independent ~2-3% excess-buoyancy hypothesis (THESIS_PLAN.md 1a).
BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 32, 15, 15 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 1, 0 >;   // [Claude, 2026-10-08] periodic in x and y
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             50000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots_b3_r075_s32_100k_eqfull_pxy_sigma0_tau051_100k;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <192, 90, 120>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 10.0;   // nominal (doubled basin)
   floorHeightFactor  0.01;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0;
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   surfaceTensionOverride 0;   // [Claude, 2026-10-09] _sigma0: Laplace pressure off
   relaxationRateOverride 1.96078431;   // [Claude, 2026-10-09] _tau051: tau 0.51
   enableWetting          false;
   timesteps              100000;
   Re                     3100;
   Fr                     1.31;
   We                     15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits      true;         // keep physical constants valid while U = 0; viscosity=0.000214026 fixed
   gravityOverride        5.06585e-05;  // solved for g_SI = 9.81 m/s^2 against job 3952542's dx_SI/dt_SI (see header)
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 2;   // FIX (2026-09-29): domainSize doubled -> bedCopies must double too, or avgParticleDiameter/dx_SI/dt_SI silently
   bedCopiesInY 2;   // rescale (getAvgDiameterScalingFactor, Utility.h) and gravityOverride no longer means g_SI=9.81. See job 4273521's own
                     // failure (avgParticleDiameter came out 12.0029 instead of 6.00146) and its retraction in THESIS_PLAN.md.
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.97;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

FloatingBoxes
{
   FloatingBox
   {
      // Bogner-like free box: s=18 (18 x 36 x 18), roll about Y only (pitch/yaw pinned), heave + X/Y translation FREE, heel seed 2.86 deg
      position             < 96, 45, 52.085 >;
      halfExtents          < 16, 32, 16 >;
      densityRatio         0.75;
      settlingSteps        0;
      initialTiltAngleDeg  2.86;
      comOffsetZ           0;
      pinPosition          false;
      pinRotation          true;
      pinRotationAxes      < 1, 0, 1 >;
   }
}

ModelParameters
{
   seedSkipObstacleNeighbours false;   // [Claude, 2026-10-08] pre-2026-10-01 seeding
   strictBognerClassification true;   // [Claude, 2026-10-08] _strict: Bogner's rule literally
   logMomentumBudget true;   // [Claude, 2026-10-09] _strict_mom: [MOMENTUM-BUDGET] diagnostic
   pdfReconstructionModel        OnlyMissing;
   pdfRefillingModel             EquilibriumRefilling;
   excessMassDistributionModel   EvenlyNewInterfaceFallbackLiquid;
   curvatureModel                FiniteDifferenceMethod;
   useSimpleMassExchange         false;
   cellConversionThreshold       1e-2;
   cellConversionForceThreshold  1e-1;
   useBognerReconstruction       true;
   useFillWeighting              true;
   useBognerThreePhaseMEM        true;
   useMemOnlyBuoyancy            true;
   repairDegenerateObstaclePdfs  false;   // Option B (obstacle-cell repair guard) OFF
   seedStreamPdfCloneOnFirstUse  false;   // Option A (scratch PDF clone seeding) OFF

   logDensityColumn              true;
   densityColumnBaseFolder       density-column;
   densityColumnX                5;
   densityColumnY                45;
   logDensityColumnStartStep     98000;
   logDensityColumnEndStep       99999;

   // fill-integrated water height on a 12 x 3 grid of columns (x = 4, 12, ..., 92; y = 7.5, 22.5, 37.5) every 250 steps over the WHOLE run
   logWaterHeight                true;
   waterHeightBaseFolder         water-height;
   waterHeightGridX              12;
   waterHeightGridY              3;
   waterHeightEveryNSteps        250;
}

EvaluationParameters
{
   performanceLogFrequency 10000;
   evaluationFrequency     250;
   baseFolderName          eval;
}

StabilityChecker
{
   checkFrequency 0;
   streamOutput   false;
   vtkOutput      true;
}

BoundaryParameters
{
   Border { direction T;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
   Border { direction B;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
}

MeshOutputParameters
{
   writeFrequency 0;
   baseFolder     mesh-out;
}

VTK
{
   // [Claude, 2026-10-08] whole domain, velocity + fill_level + mapped_flag, discrete steps over the full run
   fluid_field
   {
      writeFrequency       0;
      ghostLayers          0;
      baseFolder           vtk-out;
      samplingResolution   1;
      useMPIIO false;
      writers
      {
         velocity;
         fill_level;
         mapped_flag;
      }
      before_functions { gas_cell_zero_setter; }
   }
   fluid_field_snapshots
   {
      writeFrequency       1;
      ghostLayers          0;
      baseFolder           vtk-out;
      samplingResolution   1;
      useMPIIO false;
      steps "0,250,500,1000,2000,4000,8000,12000,16000,20000,24000,28000,32000,36000,40000,50000,60000,70000,80000,90000,99999";
      writers
      {
         velocity;
         fill_level;
         mapped_flag;
      }
      before_functions { gas_cell_zero_setter; }
   }
   domain_decomposition
   {
      writeFrequency             0;
      baseFolder                 vtk-out;
      outputDomainDecomposition  true;
   }
}
